# SUGGESTED .dockerignore for movieLinks-landing
#
# NOT APPLIED -- the MovieLinks repo is treated as read-only by this kit.
# To adopt it in the real project:
#     cp recommendations/dockerignore.suggested ../../MovieLinks/movieLinks-landing/.dockerignore
#
# Why: movieLinks-landing currently has no .dockerignore, so `docker build .`
# ships the entire working tree (~947MB: node_modules 606M, dist 128M,
# .git 92M) as build context, and `COPY . .` in the builder stage bakes it
# into that layer. With this file the context drops to the source that is
# actually needed for `npm ci && ng build`.
#
# (This kit's build.sh sidesteps the problem without touching the repo, by
# piping `git archive HEAD` in as the build context.)

# dependencies -- reinstalled inside the image by `npm ci`
node_modules
**/node_modules

# build output -- regenerated inside the image by `npm run build`
dist
.angular
*.tsbuildinfo

# version control / CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# local env & editor noise
.env
.env.*
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# logs & caches
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.npm
coverage

# docs & container config not needed at build time
README.md
CLAUDE.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
